# Titan: let TrustKernel make its secure storage, added by 65-extra-init.
#
# The same problem as trustkernel-unencrypted.rc solves on the Titan Pocket, in
# the older shape of the Titan's Android 10 vendor. Its trustkernel.rc makes
# /data/vendor/t6 (and fs/, app/) only on vendor.trustkernel.fs.state=ready,
# which it sets from the ro.crypto.state triggers for "unencrypted" and
# "encrypted". Under Halium vold reports "unsupported", so none fires and teed
# has nowhere to keep a TA's storage. On 12 Nov 2026 the fingerprint stack
# (vendor.chipsailing.fingerprint@1.0-service, on the TrustKernel TEE) sat in
# tee_supp_cmd() from its first second; the standard fingerprint HAL waited on
# it, did not even answer a ping, and biomd timed out on every start. Setting
# the two properties by hand made the directories at once, but did not free the
# call already waiting, hence doing it here, before anything asks.
#
# The Pocket's vendor uses "prepare" where this one uses "ready"; mode 1 is the
# one both set for an unencrypted /data.
on property:ro.crypto.state=unsupported
    setprop vendor.trustkernel.fs.mode 1
    setprop vendor.trustkernel.fs.state ready
